Description: opengl: Integrate the area of a stereo eye for any shrink
 A stereo eye drawn smaller than its resolution was sampled bilinearly up to
 a 2:1 reduction and integrated over the covered texels only beyond it, so a
 1.5x shrink aliased: each pixel took the nearest four texels instead of the
 area it covers. Every shrink, on either axis, now integrates that area,
 clamped to the eye; an axis that is not shrunk covers one texel, which is
 bilinear, and an eye drawn at its size or larger is still sampled
 bilinearly.
 .
 The downscale test gains a 1.5x shrink of its pattern and of an address
 fixture (every sample carries its eye, column and row, so the ramps jump at
 256), also shrunk in one axis while magnified in the other, against the
 exact area average; the 1.5x rows failed before.
